  "nl_text": "The database schema rschema_0122 is used to store information related to customer inquiries and conversations. It consists of six tables: conversation, message, inquiry, organization, security_base_record, and customer.\nThe conversation table stores information about each conversation, including the conversation ID, customer ID, creation time, last update time, and a foreign key reference to the security_base_record table. The message table stores information about each message in a conversation, including the message ID, conversation ID, content, send time, and status. The inquiry table stores information about each customer inquiry, including the customer ID, inquiry category, inquiry content, status, creation time, and end time. The organization table stores information about each organization, including the organization ID, organization name, phone number, avatar, location, email, description, homepage link, and image link. The security_base_record table stores encrypted information related to the organization, including the base ID, encrypted information, record creation time, and record update time. The customer table stores information about each customer, including the customer ID, name, contact information, and foreign key reference to the organization table.\nEach table has its own primary key, and some tables have foreign key constraints that reference other tables. For example, the conversation table has a foreign key constraint that references the security_base_record table, and the message table has a foreign key constraint that references the conversation table. The inquiry table has a composite primary key consisting of creation time and customer ID, and the customer table has a foreign key constraint that references the organization table.\nOverall, the schema is designed to store and manage customer inquiries and conversations, as well as information about the organizations and customers involved.",
  "gold_question": "The Customer Relationship Management (CRM) or Customer Service system is used to manage customer inquiries, conversation records, and organization information. Its main features include:\n1.Conversation Management: Records basic information about each conversation, including Conversation ID, Customer ID, Organization ID, Creation Time, Last Update Time, and baseId.\n2.Inquiry Management: Records customer inquiry information, including the status (open, closed, draft), category, content, creation time, and end time of the inquiry.\n3.Organization Information Management: Records the basic information of organizations, such as phone number, avatar, location, email, description, homepage link, and image link. Supports detailed management and updating of organization information, ensuring each organization has a unique phone number and avatar. Customers belong to specific organizations.\n4.Data Security: Ensures each conversation is linked to a secure base record, including baseId, encrypted information, creation time, and update time to enhance system security.\nEach customer has a unique Customer ID, name, and contact information.\nEach inquiry may involve multiple customers.\nEach conversation may involve multiple customers and multiple organizations.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0122.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0122\nCREATE TABLE `conversation` (\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_update_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `base_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`conversation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `conversation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`base_id`) REFERENCES `security_base_record` (`base_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `conversation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message` (\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `send_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`conversation_id`) REFERENCES `conversation` (`conversation_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `inquiry` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `inquiry_category` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `inquiry_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`creation_time`, `customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `inquiry_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `organization` (\n  `organization_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `organization_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `homepage_link` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_link` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`organization_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `security_base_record` (\n  `base_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `encrypted_info` text NOT NULL,\n  `record_creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `record_update_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`base_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `organization_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`organization_id`) REFERENCES `organization` (`organization_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
